  "custom_ai_disclosure": "<p>AI tooling (Claude) was used as a research and coding assistant during development,\nalways under human direction:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Reverse-engineering support</strong> — decompiling and digging through the game’s assemblies\nto find the right systems to build on (the BTR’s passenger/seat handling, EFT’s physics\nscheduler, lamp and audio systems), so the mod uses the same mechanisms the game itself\nuses instead of fragile hacks.</li>\n<li><strong>Code drafting and debugging</strong> — implementation drafts and log analysis during the\nbuild-test-fix loop.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All feature decisions, in-game testing, tuning (driving feel, camera, seat and light\nplacement), asset selection and preparation, and release validation were done by hand.\nEvery change shipped only after being tested in the game; several AI-proposed approaches\nwere rejected or reworked based on those tests. The 3D model, sounds, and artwork are not\nAI-generated.</p>\n",
